@startuml FRQ-CON-16.1-device-state
' Stanje uređaja — zauzeće i smjer.
' Gledište: ponašanje. Publika: implementator, tester.
' Prikaz, ne izvor istine (D-13) — izvor je FRQ-CON-16.1 §5–§6.
' Preslikavanje na ConnectionState temeljne konekcije je u bilješci N2.
title FRQ-CON-16.1 — device state: exclusive claim and half-duplex direction

[*] --> Registered : factory (BR-01)

Registered --> Resolving : create_connection()
Resolving --> Failed_NotFound : zero matches
Resolving --> Failed_Ambiguous : more than one match\n(never "take the first", BR-02)
Resolving --> Claiming : exactly one match

Claiming --> Failed_Busy : held by another process\n(enumeration works, claim fails)
Claiming --> Failed_Permission : no rights on the device node
Claiming --> Verifying : claimed

Verifying --> Failed_ProfileMismatch : profile disagrees with reported,\nor a value outside the profile (BR-11)
Verifying --> Failed_Unsupported : mechanism does not\nsupport the model (BR-14)
Verifying --> Failed_OutOfRange : centre frequency outside\nthe profile range (BR-15)
Verifying --> Configured : profile confirmed

Configured --> Connected : parameters applied\nand READ BACK (BR-05)

state Connected {
  [*] --> Receiving : direction = RECEIVE
  Receiving --> Idle : stop
  Idle --> Receiving : direction = RECEIVE
  Idle --> Transmitting : direction = TRANSMIT\n<b>only with authorisation</b> (NFRQ-SEC-07)
  Transmitting --> Idle : stop

  note right of Transmitting #FFCDD2
    Half duplex: Receiving and Transmitting
    exclude each other (BR-12). A receiver
    never enters here — its profile has no
    TRANSMIT direction.
  end note
}

Connected --> Interrupted : device left the bus (BR-09)
Connected --> Released : disconnect()
Interrupted --> Released : disconnect() (idempotent)
Released --> [*]

Failed_NotFound --> [*]
Failed_Ambiguous --> [*]
Failed_Busy --> [*]
Failed_Permission --> [*]
Failed_ProfileMismatch --> [*]
Failed_Unsupported --> [*]
Failed_OutOfRange --> [*]

note as N1
  Seven failure classes differ by <b>type</b>,
  not only by message (FRQ-CON-16.1 k.6).
  "Present" and "available" are two states:
  Resolving succeeds while Claiming fails.
end note

note as N2
  <b>Mapping to ConnectionState</b>
  Resolving … Configured = CREATING
  Configured = CREATED
  Connected = CONNECTING / CONNECTED
  Released = CLOSED; Failed_* = FAILED
end note
@enduml
